2026-10-23T21:59:39.6933052Z # --no-renames, and it is not cosmetic: a rename is reported by its
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6933558Z # DESTINATION only, so moving CLAUDE.md to RENAMED.md yields a list
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6934041Z # matching no glob and the approval gate would not fire on the change
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6934550Z # that removed a policy file. Measured both ways before wiring it.
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6935099Z git diff --no-renames --name-only "$PR_BASE...$PR_HEAD" > /tmp/pr-files.txt
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6935519Z wc -l < /tmp/pr-files.txt
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6936157Z # The same diff less its additions: what the base already had. A
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6936755Z # reporter that grades `main` is exempt from `## Red checks` only
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6937246Z # while the diff touches none of its inputs, and a delivery row the
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6937779Z # pull request ADDS (its own) is not one; a row it edits or deletes is.
2026-10-23T21:59:39.6938388Z git diff --no-renames --name-only --diff-filter=a "$PR_BASE...$PR_HEAD" > /tmp/pr-existing.txt
